{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 32, :comments ["<b>Come, let us.</b> It should have said לכי (feminine), and it said לכה in the masculine form, because the elder sister instructed the younger to do a man's deed — for it is the way of the male to conquer the female and to make the verbal demand, which is not fitting for the female, as the Sages interpreted (Genesis 1): ״וכבשוה״ — and it is written וכבשה (without the vav): a man's way is to conquer, and a woman's way is not to conquer. And from what they said, ״and there is no man in the earth to come in unto us,״ their intention is clarified: because the males were lacking from the generation, she commanded her sister to conduct herself in the manner of conquest and demand; and since she altered the way of the world and the norms of proper conduct, Scripture likewise altered in her the word לכה, which is the masculine form, just as she altered the way of the female for that of the male." "<b>And the correct interpretation</b> in my opinion is that the supplementary ה (heh) in the word לכה is because the letter ה alludes to the attribute of Judgment (דין), in the manner of what is said to Moses our teacher, peace be upon him (Exodus 3:10): ״ועתה לכה ואשלחך אל פרעה״, concerning which Scripture said (ibid.): ״וזה לך האות״ — this is the sign of the ה, which is in the word לכה, and wine alludes to the attribute of Judgment; therefore the masters of truth said: one does not recite a blessing over wine unless one has put water into it. And behold, the daughters grasp the spindle of their mother, who caused the man to sin, and this is the opinion of the one who says in the Midrash: she pressed grapes and brought them to him, and corresponding to this sin she was punished with the blood of menstruation, for the appearance is the same, and he explained from it by that same appearance. And this is the secret of the language by which Scripture called the species of wine in the language of blood, as it is written (Deuteronomy 32:14): ״ודם ענב תשתה חמר״. And it is written (Genesis 49:11): ״כבס ביין לבושו ובדם ענבים סותה״, and the supplementary letters ה״י are not for nothing, and this is what the Sages said: the man emits white and the woman emits red." "<b>And behold,</b> the sin of the mother and the sin of the daughters in this deed are equal, by means of wine, which is the cause of the world's evils. And perhaps the pleonasm of <b>את אבינו</b> (our father) — את אבינו הראשון, the first father — alludes to the fact that he too drank by means of a woman. And the conclusion."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {1 "Reading והיין (and wine) with most witnesses; the logical flow — wine alluding to the attribute of Judgment — supports this over the printed והיין which may be a typographical variant.", 2 "Reading והבן ('and the conclusion,' i.e., the matter is concluded/understood) as a fixed Rabbinic formula closing the comment, though it may conceivably be an abbreviation for והבן זאת or similar; the trailing open-endedness is retained."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:13:54.921053034Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}